RT                LINCOLN\n\nIN NORTHEAST COLORADO\n\nADAMS                 ARAPAHOE              DENVER\nDOUGLAS               LOGAN                 MORGAN\nPHILLIPS              SEDGWICK              WASHINGTON\nWELD\n\nTHIS INCLUDES THE CITIES OF AKRON, AURORA, CASTLE ROCK,\nCENTENNIAL, DENVER, DENVER INTERNATIONAL AIRPORT, ELIZABETH,\nFORT MORGAN, GREELEY, HOLYOKE, JULESBURG, KIOWA, LIMON, PARKER,\nSTERLING, THORNTON, WESTMINSTER, AND WINDSOR.","ends":"2026-08-16T21:00:00-06:00","severity":"Severe","areaDesc":"Adams, CO; Arapahoe, CO; Denver, CO; Douglas, CO; Elbert, CO; Lincoln, CO; Logan, CO; Morgan, CO; Phillips, CO; Sedgwick, CO; Washington, CO; Weld, CO","id":"urn:oid:2.49.0.1.840.0.b1e6f8e2ba2bd466551a7c90038f7d5dc203b905.001.1","url":"https://api.weather.gov/alerts/urn:oid:2.49.0.1.840.0.b1e6f8e2ba2bd466551a7c90038f7d5dc203b905.001.1"},{"event":"Flood Advisory","headline":"Flood Advisory issued August 16 at 1:35PM MDT until August 16 at 4:30PM MDT by NWS Denver CO","description":"* WHAT...Flooding caused by excessive rainfall is expected.\n\n* WHERE...Southeastern Douglas County in northeastern Colorado...\n\n* WHEN...Until 430 PM MDT.\n\n* IMPACTS...Minor flooding in low-lying and poor drainage areas.\n\n* ADDITIONAL DETAILS...\n\n- At 135 PM MDT, Doppler radar indicated heavy rain due to\nthunderstorms. Minor flooding is ongoing or expected to begin\nshortly in the advisory area. Between 1 and 1.25 inches of rain\nhave fallen.\n\n- This includes the following streams and drainages...\nElk Creek, West Cherry Creek, Running Creek, Antelope Creek,\nCherry Creek, Crowfoot Creek, East Cherry Creek, Lake Gulch and\nCarpenter Creek. Additional rainfall amounts up to 0.5 inches are\nexpected over the area. This additional rain will result in minor\nflooding.\n\n- Some locations that will experience flooding include...\nGreenland.","ends":"2026-08-16T16:30:00-06:00","severity":"Minor","areaDesc":"Douglas, CO","id":"urn:oid:2.49.0.1.840.0.f8dfd65a9111ae8b572c1755